  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    R, C = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    visited = [[False] * C for _ in range(R)]\n    dirs = [(1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, 1), (0, -1)]\n\n    for r in range(R):\n        for c in range(C):\n            if grid[r][c] == 5 and not visited[r][c]:\n                # Collect 4-connected component of 5s\n                stack = [(r, c)]\n                visited[r][c] = True\n                min_r = max_r = r\n                min_c = max_c = c\n\n                while stack:\n                    cr, cc = stack.pop()\n                    if cr < min_r:\n                        min_r = cr\n                    if cr > max_r:\n                        max_r = cr\n                    if cc < min_c:\n                        min_c = cc\n                    if cc > max_c:\n                        max_c = cc\n                    for dr, dc in dirs:\n                        nr, nc = cr + dr, cc + dc\n                        if 0 <= nr < R and 0 <= nc < C and not visited[nr][nc] and grid[nr][nc] == 5:\n                            visited[nr][nc] = True\n                            stack.append((nr, nc))\n\n                # Need at least 2 rows and 2 cols to have an interior\n                if max_r - min_r < 1 or max_c - min_c < 1:\n                    continue\n\n                # Verify the bounding-box perimeter is entirely 5\n                ok = True\n                for cc in range(min_c, max_c + 1):\n                    if grid[min_r][cc] != 5 or grid[max_r][cc] != 5:\n                        ok = False\n                        break\n                if not ok:\n                    continue\n                for rr in range(min_r, max_r + 1):\n                    if grid[rr][min_c] != 5 or grid[rr][max_c] != 5:\n                        ok = False\n                        break\n                if not ok:\n                    continue\n\n                # Gather interior zeros\n                zero_cells = []\n                zero_set = set()\n                for rr in range(min_r + 1, max_r):\n                    for cc in range(min_c + 1, max_c):\n                        if grid[rr][cc] == 0:\n                            zero_cells.append((rr, cc))\n                            zero_set.add((rr, cc))\n\n                if not zero_cells:\n                    continue\n\n                visited0 = set()\n                for zr, zc in zero_cells:\n                    if (zr, zc) in visited0:\n                        continue\n                    # BFS this 4-connected zero region\n                    q = [(zr, zc)]\n                    visited0.add((zr, zc))\n                    comp = [(zr, zc)]\n                    cz_min_r = cz_max_r = zr\n                    cz_min_c = cz_max_c = zc\n\n                    while q:\n                        cr, cc = q.pop()\n                        for dr, dc in dirs:\n                            nr, nc = cr + dr, cc + dc\n                            if (nr, nc) in zero_set and (nr, nc) not in visited0:\n                                visited0.add((nr, nc))\n                                q.append((nr, nc))\n                                comp.append((nr, nc))\n                                if nr < cz_min_r:\n                                    cz_min_r = nr\n                                if nr > cz_max_r:\n                                    cz_max_r = nr\n                                if nc < cz_min_c:\n                                    cz_min_c = nc\n                                if nc > cz_max_c:\n                                    cz_max_c = nc\n\n                    h = cz_max_r - cz_min_r + 1\n                    w = cz_max_c - cz_min_c + 1\n                    if h == w and len(comp) == h * w:\n                        for rr, cc in comp:\n                            out[rr][cc] = 2\n\n    return out\n```",
